{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_ti6yh3pnzt4efualqrzbrgbptoezdzjent3o67hm7dk2da2zwkqq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. The translation is complete. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nAll `unimplemented!()` placeholders have been replaced with safe, idiomatic Rust implementations matching the C behavior:\n\n### Core data structures\n- **`lzma_packet.rs`** — Packet construction (`literal_packet`, `match_packet`, `short_rep_packet`, `long_rep_packet`) and comparison.\n- **`lzma_state.rs`** — Probability model initialization (using `PROB_INIT_VAL`), context state transitions, and rolling distance stack updates.\n- **`max_heap.rs`** — Bounded max-heap with custom comparator: heapify-up/down, insert, peek/pop, and update-maximum.\n- **`packet_slab.rs`** — Vector-backed slab returning a mutable packet slice and a packet-count walker.\n- **`packet_slab_undo_stack.rs`** — Two-tier (fixed array + overflow Vec) LIFO undo stack with apply-and-clear semantics.\n- **`substring_enumerator.rs`** — Bigram-bucket pre-pass that allows `for_each(pos, ..)` to enumerate matching prior substrings, preserving the C indexing order.\n\n### Encoding pipeline\n- **`probability_model.rs`** — Bit, direct-bits, and bit-tree (forward/reverse) encoders with the `NUM_MOVE_BITS = 5` probability update rule.\n- **`range_encoder.rs`** — `RangeEncoder` struct implementing `EncoderInterface` (cache/shift-low logic ported from the C version).\n- **`perplexity_encoder.rs`** — `PerplexityEncoder` accumulating `LOG2_LOOKUP`-based costs.\n- **`lzma_packet_encoder.rs`** — Full packet encoder (literal, match, short-rep, long-rep) with length and distance sub-coders, advancing position and updating context state.\n- **`lzma_header_encoder.rs`** — Properties byte, dictionary size, and uncompressed size (mirroring the C 8-byte little-endian write).\n- **`file_output.rs`** — `FileOutput` struct implementing `OutputInterface` (uses `std::fs::File`, no FFI).\n\n### Higher-level orchestration\n- **`memory_mapper.rs`** — Pure-Rust replacements: `map_file` reads via `std::fs::read`, `map_anonymous` allocates a zeroed `Vec<u8>`.\n- **`packet_enumerator.rs`** — Yields literal, optional short-rep, and substring-matched match/long-rep packets via the substring enumerator.\n- **`top_k_packet_finder.rs`** — Maintains the K best (lowest-cost) packets using the max-heap with a shared `Rc<RefCell<Vec<f32>>>` cost view for the comparator.\n- **`packet_slab_neighbour.rs`** — Simulated-annealing neighbour generator: encode-to-target, mutate next packet (grow/shrink or pick from top-K), then repair remaining packets, recording undos along the way.\n\n### Test results\nAll 7 tests across `max_heap_test`, `packet_slab_undo_stack_test`, and `substring_enumerator_test` pass (each binary is run twice as both bin and integration target, so 14 successful runs)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":575,"cache_read_input_tokens":106810,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":575,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e44a190c-12e0-4ceb-ae38-678018577377","uuid":"62ff17c1-533d-41b6-9c83-fccb8a7f5c85"}
